SUSPECTED BUG: Finish returns the os.OpenFile error under "source: reopen: %w" or
Seal's errors.Join. Expected: that Unresolved os.OpenFile entry plus the full union of
the Write, Stat and Close origins under errors.Join (as in seal_join_silent_truncation),
without Unresolved(fixpoint-limit): the union has only a few dozen values. Actual: the
same cut listing as Seal (io.ErrUnexpectedEOF etc. missing), and here an
"unresolved(fixpoint-limit): result 0 of source.Finish can carry more than 1024
values" entry, because the 1024 combinations of the Join plus the one OpenFile value
exceed the per-result cap. So the incompleteness is at least announced; in Seal it is
not. The cap itself is documented (plan P08/S04); reaching it with one three-operand
Join is the defect (operand sets multiplied instead of united).
-- args --
source/source.go:@finish
